{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina","id":804918,"title":"Homebrew G-M Numina","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-09T19:09:53-08:00","id":804918,"title":"Homebrew G-M Numina","content":"Enjoy:<br /> <br /> <b>Authority</b><br /> Servants of the of the G-M have long appropriated mortal power structures for their own needs. The occult physics of this Numina form the basis of the demonic embed Authorized, but Angels benefit from millennia of reinforcement by Infrastructure, occult matrices, and the pycho-social programming that modern humans are exposed to from birth.<br /> <br /> By spending an essence to activate this Numina an angel become a member of an appropriate agency, group or corporate entity. Witnesses don\u2019t just believe that the angel has authority, the angel <i>genuinely has</i> the franchise to act as they see fit. When an angel walks through the doors of Deva corp, she pulls out her security badge (created by the Numina as a side effect) the security guard remembers her from the company picnic last week, the secretary reminds her of a meeting at 10 and there\u2019s an office on the forth floor with her name on it. If the angel enters a crime scene then there's an FBI badge in her pocket, her photo and records will be on file at the FBI head-quarters in Washington, and there\u2019s a supervisor at the Denver field office who mentored her. Some of the police on the scene remember her from a previous case. If the angel requires a warrant, she can produce one immediately from her brief case, and the relevant judge will remember having signed it last night.<br /> <br /> In game terms, the Angel gains status in an organization equal to it\u2019s rank (or less, if it want to be less conspicuous) and the Connected condition. Trying to use this Numina in areas claimed by werewolves as territory usually triggers unexpected and sometimes lethal effects.<br /> <br /> <b>Eyes Everywhere</b><br /> The modern world is filled with mechanical eyes: the ATM, the cameras on the stop lights, police dashboard cameras. An angel with this Numina gains the ability to see out 4 + Power cameras per scene (no cost at the start of a scene). These cameras must be within Rank miles, and the Angel must have at least a general idea of their location. \u201cThe Cellphone of Ms. Ice, whatever cover she\u2019s in\u201d is no good, but \u201can ATM camera near Main Street and Elm Boulevard\u201d is fine. An Angel can pay 1 essence to select new cameras, abiding by the same restrictions as before. These cameras are added to list of ones it\u2019s connected to.<br /> Viewing multiple cameras never impacts the angels ability to be aware of its surroundings. \u201cParallel processing\u201d is an inherent part of this Numina.<br /> <br /> <br /> Dev Notes: Was inspired by Person of Interest with some of the antics of Martine and Samaritan. Authority has some overlap with Given the design notes of the STG outline, there was a note about trying to avoid Numina that had extended rolls or took place in the background. Authority gives a hands on approach, allowing an angel to take control of investigations (either directly or in the background courtesy of implant mission), walk into evidence lockers, and chat with senators, CEOs and bishops.<br /> Eyes Everywhere is surveillance power modeled on the endowment for network zero, with a few tweaks. In combination with the Space Incept a moderately ranked angel can swiftly get access to dozens or even hundreds of surveillance feeds to hunt its quarry. More to follow as I think of them, feel free to comment or add your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":".  Edit: changed Eyes Everwhere to use power instead of rank to make it more essence efficient. 02-07-2016, 01:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T21:38:39-08:00","id":805004,"title":"","content":"Oh my god. If you stated Samaritan as a Rank 5 Analyst or Psychopomp, it would be absolutely terrifying with Eyes Everywhere. And not just the Space Incept, but the Units Incept as well. <br /> <br /> As such, Samaritan as a GM Angel could control fifteen cameras at once over a radius of 40 miles. That is really quite terrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T21:42:08-08:00","id":805007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=805004#post805004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh my god. If you stated Samaritan as a Rank 5 Analyst or Psychopomp,</div> </div> </div> </div>Challenge accepted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T21:52:38-08:00","id":805009,"title":"","content":"I imagine the Machine would be an Exile of identical Incarnation who has managed to hack some Infrastructure.<br /> <br /> Another thing I thought of- if the Doctor is a Demon, does that make the TARDIS a Lares?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T22:24:33-08:00","id":805019,"title":"","content":"These are definitely Numina terrifying enough to raise a Demon's paranoia scale all the way to 11. Noting this for future reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T03:58:20-08:00","id":805130,"title":"","content":"Very nice. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina#post804918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In game terms, the Angel gains status in an organization equal to it\u2019s rank (or less, if it want to be less conspicuous) and the Connected condition. Trying to use this Numina in areas claimed by werewolves as territory usually triggers unexpected and sometimes lethal effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I loved this aside, by the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T05:23:51-08:00","id":805161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=805009#post805009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing I thought of- if the Doctor is a Demon, does that make the TARDIS a Lares?</div> </div> </div> </div>The TARDIS was one of the things I thought of when designing Lares, actually, as an option for Lare-as-ally. Along with Charlie from Charlie's Angels.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T17:30:41-08:00","id":805635,"title":"","content":"Here goes:<br /> <br /> c.AI.n<br /> <br /> <b>Incarnation:</b> Analyst<br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Relentless<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Visionary<br /> <b>Rank:</b> 4<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 12, Finesse 8, Resistance 10<br /> <b>Influence: </b>Surveillance \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 10 + *<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 30 (10 species factor)<br /> <b>Defense: </b>8<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 20<br /> <b>Armor: </b><br /> <b>Numina:</b> Aggressive Meme, Eyes Everywhere, Freeze Accounts**, Holy Ground, Implant Mission, Open Investigation, Merciless Gunman**, Murder By Improbability**, Power Out<br /> <b>Incepts: </b>Delivery, Efficiency, Space, Units<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Twilight Form, Discorporate, Dataform***, Possess****<br /> <b>Max Essence:</b> 25<br /> <b>Ban:</b> c.AI.n must pursue (through agents, if need be) any crime it sees. Being a demon is automatically a crime for the purposes of this Ban.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Proof that an executed individual was innocent. Embeds or exploits that damage or erase data are treated as lethal weapons if used against c.AI.n<br /> <br /> <b>Other:</b> cult \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 ( Loyal agents inserted into any number of espionage and law enforcement agencies)<br /> <br /> * c.AI.n can only exist inside material object, so corpus will depend on what it is possessing<br /> **as per the Embed or Exploit. Merciless Gun can only be used through Delivery by a friendly agent.<br /> *** Spend 3 essence to manifest as data, treated as the Dataform<br /> **** c.AI.n is limited to occupying technical objects such as computers, security systems, unmanned drones and spy satellites.<br /> <br /> Description: c.AI.n is an unusual hunter-angel that is more akin to a siege weapon than an actual hunter. The G-M deploys c.AI.n when its needs make war on the Unchained. Using hundreds if not thousands of CCTV feeds, radio frequencies, cellphone cameras, c.AI.n begins a systematic hunt for all signs of deviance, mundane crimes result in police and security forces dispatches. More cunning targets might invite c.AI.n to dispatch one of its cultists to carry out an execution.<br /> <br /> When a demonic ring or agency is discovered, c.AI.n goes into full attack. Open Investigation brings in multiple federal agencies and data form infiltrates school and workplace computers, find out where demons work and where their children go to school.<br /> <br /> Whenever one of c.AI.n\u2019s agents executes a criminal in the view of exactly 4 security cameras, that soul becomes a human sacrifice to fuel c.AI.n\u2019s occult matrix.<br /> <br /> While c.AI.n nothing but loyal to the G-M, it has taken to running calculations, simulations of ways that human society might be improved\u2026 for their own good of course. <br /> <br /> Notes: I limited myself to rank four to make this angel deadly because of smart design and tactics, rather than just crushing players with huge dice-pools. With enough limitations, players have the ability to out maneuver and out think and enemy.<br /> <br /> Nine numina is a hard limit when you have something as flavorful as a Samaritan knock-off. Eyes Everywhere is the showcase, to show how utterly broken the right combination of Incepts can be; by my math c.AI.n can affect either 46 or 78 security systems with a single essence, depending on how you want to fiddle with order of operations. <br /> Freeze Account is is nice way of hounding a quarry and blackmailing allies. Merciless Gunman is based on Samaritan/The Machine\u2019s \u201cgod mode.\u201d With Delivery it can be used to covertly execute criminals\u2026 or turn a SWAT team into a nightmare that cuts apart demons. Holy Ground + Possess + Murder by Improbability gives it a nice control of the. Left hand-spanner disables cars and firearms and Power Out lets it do <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ln7QK4CUtXw\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.<br /> <br /> Since the Space incept allows a numen to operate on line of sight, I wanted c.AI.n able to posses UAVs and spy satellites for a nice modern update to Enemy of the State. I was going to add blast to super charge electrical systems and blow up gas mains, but something had to go and that was already covered by Murder by Improbability.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T17:54:52-08:00","id":805648,"title":"","content":"Wait, did I miss something?<br /> <br /> What's an Incept?<br /> <br /> (oh god the retroactive changes are happening again)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T18:03:56-08:00","id":805653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=805648#post805648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's an Incept?</div> </div> </div> </div>New Angel cheats from the Demon Storyteller's Guide. (From what I infer, not possessing such a tome yet...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T18:15:54-08:00","id":805659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=805648#post805648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, did I miss something?<br /> <br /> What's an Incept?<br /> <br /> (oh god the retroactive changes are happening again)</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I've seen, it's a new thing from the Demon Storyteller Guide. I'm guessing that they're some sort of Meta-Numina?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T18:35:23-08:00","id":805671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=805659#post805659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I've seen, it's a new thing from the Demon Storyteller Guide. I'm guessing that they're some sort of Meta-Numina?</div> </div> </div> </div>Activating an Incept is a big deal and you'll know when it happens.<br /> <br /> They modify angels in ways like &quot;the angel can make its Numina last longer, take effect sooner, or activate on a time delay,&quot; &quot;the angel applies its Rank as a fuel surcharge as a non-autofail stipulation to any powers that would affect it even if the user doesn't know they'd be affecting the angel, and can recover Essence through sources of Aether that aren't demons,&quot; and &quot;the angel can use its Incepts to enhance another entity, and can create a portal to any other part of the cosmology like the Shadow or the Abyss.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T18:46:24-08:00","id":805678,"title":"","content":"Incepts are the God Machine's admin codes to reality. They allow some truly bonkers powers. Though, I don't think the most bonkers combinations have yet been found (based on this forum's posts).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T19:33:30-08:00","id":805714,"title":"","content":"Have 3 new Numina that are very useful for Angels. Feedback is appreciated.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Branding: </b>This Numen forms the basis for Embeds like Tag And Release and Special Someone, and Exploits like Inflict Stigmata. However, Angels use it to overload a Demon's Primum, resulting in a temporary Glitch. The Demon must be within the Angel's [Rank x 5] in yards, under direct observation (no cameras or the Eyes Everywhere Numen posted above) and the Angel must know the target is a Demon. Spend 2 Essence and roll Power + Finesse vs the Demon's Resolve + Composure. A success causes a minor Glitch and an exceptional success causes a major Glitch. The duration is one hour per success on the activation roll. By spending 4 Essence + 1 willpower point, a success causes a major Glitch, an exceptional success causes a catastrophic Glitch, and the duration becomes one day per success on the activation roll (up to the Angel's Rank x 2). Despite the Numen's name, the Glitch can be a Brand or Tell, but only an Emanation if the Demon's Primum is 6 or more. Besides that, the Angel has no control over what the Glitch will be. Only Angels of Rank 3 or more may have this Numen. If the Demon has the Monkeywrencher Merit (Flowers Of Hell page 129), he may use it against this Numen, and the Compromise roll is considered an exceptional success with 3 successes.<br /> <br /> I came up with this after re-reading the section in the core about Glitches, which mentions that some supernatural powers can cause them. However, I did not find any examples. Should I allow the Angel to further specify what the Glitch will be by paying additional Essence, or is the element of unpredictability more interesting? Should I allow other ephemeral beings to have this Numen, such as spirits of truth, curiosity and mischief that can use a variant which causes something like the Tells of Wolf-Blooded (maybe this variant can also make the target appear to be Possessed or Claimed)?<br /> <br /> <b>Healer: </b>This Numen forms the basis for Embeds like On The Mend and Exploits like Halo. With no Essence cost or roll, a number of individuals equal to the Angel's [Rank x 2] within [Rank x 5] yards of the Angel heal their wounds [Rank + 1] times faster (the Angel can exempt anyone it can perceive directly from this effect and apply it again at will). The Angel is capable of touching a wounded individual and spending Essence to cure their wounds faster. They may spend 1 Essence to heal 1 lethal damage or 2 bashing damage. They may heal as many wounds in this way per turn as allowed by their Rank*. Alternatively, they can spend 3 Essence + 1 willpower point to downgrade a number of aggravated damage equal to their [Rank + 1] into lethal. This healing removes Tilts like Blinded, Deafened, Arm Wrack and Leg Wrack, even if caused by aggravated damage. They may spend 1 Essence as an instant action to cure moderate instances of Sick and Poisoned, as well as Drugged. Healing grave instances of the first two Tilts costs 2 Essence. This Numen cannot cure mental afflictions, such as those represented by the Madness, Broken and Fugue Conditions.<br /> <br /> *I house-rule that the maximum Essence Per Turn that an ephemeral being can spend is [Rank x 3]. I came up with this Numen after realizing that I didn't know how much Influence: Healing actually heals. Having this Numen is also more cost effective, as it allows the ephemeral being to heal multiple individuals without having to invest 5 dots in Influence: Healing, which would also require Rank 5. While this Numen is very tied to Biblical imagery of divine cures given to the faithful, other ephemeral beings can have it, and faith is not required (though the ephemeral being can fool mortals into thinking that it is). At your discretion, ephemeral beings of Rank 4+ may have more potent versions of this Numen that can heal more wounds with less Essence, and even cure mental afflictions.<br /> <br /> <b>Enduring:</b> This Numen forms the basis for Embeds like Just Bruised, as well as protective Demonic Form abilities. In addition to downgrading lethal damage from mundane sources into bashing, an Angel with this Numen downgrades a number of aggravated damage from supernatural or mundane-but-devastating sources equal to their [Rank + 1] into lethal. By spending 2 Essence, they can downgrade all aggravated damage into lethal, but they must pay the cost for each aggravated attack received this turn. In addition, their wounds heal [Rank + 1] times faster, with no Essence cost or roll. Only Angels of Rank 3+ can have this Numen. Banes can bypass this protection.<br /> <br /> I thought this would be a scary Numen for Destroyer Angels to have. That's pretty much it. As with the previous Numina, I see no problem with allowing other ephemeral beings to use it, but Rank 3+ should still be a requirement.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 01-11-2016, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T19:39:49-08:00","id":805716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=805161#post805161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The TARDIS was one of the things I thought of when designing Lares, actually, as an option for Lare-as-ally. Along with Charlie from Charlie's Angels.</div> </div> </div> </div> What is a Lares? In my write-up of Unchained!Doctor, I defined the TARDIS as a super Bolthole, which he could also control with the Demon House Exploit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T19:48:53-08:00","id":805720,"title":"","content":"A Lares is an Exile that has the Cover of a building or other inanimate object. They can entirely control the shape and size of the interior of said building. It's still a little fuzzy about what Angelic Covers actually are, if they're some kind of special trait not represented by game mechanics, or just an Angel using Mortal Mask, but they're there, and they're explained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T20:24:35-08:00","id":805739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=805720#post805720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Lares is an Exile that has the Cover of a building or other inanimate object. They can entirely control the shape and size of the interior of said building. It's still a little fuzzy about what Angelic Covers actually are, if they're some kind of special trait not represented by game mechanics, or just an Angel using Mortal Mask, but they're there, and they're explained.</div> </div> </div> </div> Interesting! That does sound like the TARDIS. References to the TARDIS being alive appear multiple times on the show over the years from what I've read, and it even assumed <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Doctor%27s_Wife\" target=\"_blank\"><b>a human form once.</b></a> Furthermore, it displays some miscellaneous powers that Boltholes don't have.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T18:07:15-08:00","id":810428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=805714#post805714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have 3 new Numina that are very useful for Angels. Feedback is appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>You got it.<br /> <br /> <b>Branding: </b> Conceptually, I loved this. It recalls the scene where Agent Smith deletes Neo's mouth in <i>The Matrix</i>. It's creepy and give a nice sense of body horror: not only can the angels smite you from on high, they can rip you apart on the genetic level. Also, you reference Eyes Everywhere <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Mechanically, though, it's frustrating. This Numen reveals a demon, so Spoofing applies. Then Supernatural Resistance should be added in the resistance roll. Demons use their Cover, which is typically much higher than Primum. If their Primum is higher they have the option of Supernatural Bulwark. This Numen isn't reliable unless a demon is careless enough to have a low cover and low Primum, or the angel boosts it with a few Incepts. That's built into the setting; cover is the most critical protection a demon has, so it must be robust against supernatural assault. Note that the most effective Demon-identifying Numen the setting offers works by targeting <i>everyone else</i>.<br /> <br /> Triggering glitches isn't something an angel needs to do at close range. If the angel is close enough to use this Numina and knows they're dealing with a demon, they're in a position to do more interesting (e.g. violent) things, or just drive to the demon's home and tell her family some interesting details (&quot;Did you know your wife was originally sent to run you over with a car? Funny but true.&quot; Since the angel is present in the scene, their rank would count against the compromise roll)<br /> <br /> I see the use for preventing a demon from fleeing into another cover, but this Numen feels like it should be re-worked into a tool that flushes a demon out of hiding, a techgnostic dye pack in a bank robber's bag. Maybe the angel could activate it by touching someone who has a cover-pact with the demon?<br /> <br /> <b>Healer: </b> Very useful for angels recruiting cultists, or leading them into battle. Also setting appropriate, as the GMC mentions that angels cut deals with mortals just as demons do, they're just not as savvy or as cut-throat.<br /> <br /> Three suggestions/observations:<br /> <br /> First, try trimming the word count and mechanical crunch. Most antagonist abilities in CoD are <i>very</i> sparsely described with simple mechanics to allow a story-teller to apply the effect without slowing the pace.<br /> <br /> Second, include a provision where an angel can <i>undo</i> the healing. It's thematic since the original GMC makes it clear that breaking a deal with an angel is a Very Bad Idea, and as far as the G-M is concerned, a body's health is all just data that can be manipulated, including the mystical version of &quot;ctrl+z&quot;. From a narrative perspective, it puts anyone an angel helps in exchange for service on a <i>very</i> short leash. Dealing with a sleeper or simulacra is unnerving. Dealing with a man who serves an angel because his son can die with a snap of the angel's fingers? That's chilling.<br /> <br /> Third, that this Numen covers that same ground as Regenerate from the GMC, and does more besides. Maybe Regenerate is a prerequisite for this Numen?<br /> <br /> <b>Enduring:</b> Not quite up to the other two, unfortunately. Angels, as ephemeral beings already have the ability to boast their attributes by rank + 2 by spending essence, and the main GMC already has the Numina Stalwart and Regenerate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 01-26-2016, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T00:03:05-08:00","id":814695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=805720#post805720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Lares is an Exile that has the Cover of a building or other inanimate object. They can entirely control the shape and size of the interior of said building. It's still a little fuzzy about what Angelic Covers actually are, if they're some kind of special trait not represented by game mechanics, or just an Angel using Mortal Mask, but they're there, and they're explained.</div> </div> </div> </div>Angelic covers are exactly whatever the Angel is supposed to be. They're reinforced by the God-Machine, so no amount of mundane digging will reveal them to be anything other than what they claim. A school principal who has worked there for years has always worked there for years, even if she just Outputted from an occult matrix yesterday. An angel with cover as a building will appear to have occupied that site since the records show the building was constructed, even if the God-Machine moved things around (like a Dark City) to place it there. <br /> <br /> Angelic cover doesn't follow Demon rules because of their solidity. Angels can be detected by doing things very outside cover, like throwing around Numina and unleashing their full power, but even these tend to go away with time - even quicker if it uses the Witness Protection Numen.<br /> <br /> Edit for clarity: Angelic covers are more plot device than something to be encapsulated in rules. They're impenetrable to mortals, except when they're not for plot reasons. A person on the street will never notice the building that wasn't there yesterday, except when they do because the Storyteller needs that person's unbelievable story to reach the ears of certain demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 01-23-2016, 03:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T00:36:22-08:00","id":814700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=814695#post814695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Angelic covers are more plot device than something to be encapsulated in rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the main thing that's confusing to people stems from the fact that angels are ephemeral beings who would nominally lose quite a bit of Essence on maintaining a material form for any significant length of time, which seems at odds with the multiple examples of angels operating under Covers that seem for all the world like a tailor-made body they're indefinitely possessing instead of the combination of Materialize and Mortal Mask their statblocks generally imply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T10:14:03-08:00","id":814895,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's sort of what's been bugging me. An Angel running around in a Cover constantly should be <i>haemorrhaging </i>Essence unless it is somehow perpetually getting sacrifices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T10:20:20-08:00","id":814898,"title":"","content":"Materialise stopped essence bleed, last time I checked.<br /> <br /> Also not a single angel has the Mortal Mask Numen, so clearly that's not what's happening here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 01-23-2016, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T10:24:17-08:00","id":814901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=814898#post814898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Materialise stopped essence bleed, last time I checked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Particulars of bleed notwithstanding, it also has a timer measured in hours and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806771-mortal-mask-renewable\">the nearest thing to a workaround I've managed to guess at</a> is likewise not costless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also not a single angel has the Mortal Mask Numen </div> </div> </div>This is\u2026 laughably false.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 01-23-2016, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T10:30:33-08:00","id":814907,"title":"","content":"For some, at least, the presence of Infrastructure is probably stopping the bleed. Not sure about the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T10:31:55-08:00","id":814908,"title":"","content":"Whoops, my mistake. There is at least one angel with Mortal Mask. Unfortunately he can't use it because he doesn't have <i>materialize</i>.<br /> <br /> And anyway, that's besides the point. The core book has several angels who blatantly wander round in human form and just as blatantly have no means of doing so by themselves. Ergo, angelic cover is not simply a case of using manifestations in this manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 01-23-2016, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T13:30:25-08:00","id":815001,"title":"","content":"Yes, I sympathise with the confusion. I asked the same questions when working on the DSTG. <br /> <br /> Angels performing their function don't have to worry about essence bleed. Either the G-M continually tops them up, pays the cost for them, or has some other reality hack in place. The specifics don't matter, losing Essence from simply existing isn't an angelic concern. <br /> <br /> Similarly, angels whose function requires a body simply have a body. They're either Outputted with one, or they permanently take over some poor human's shell, or they materialise. If their function requires permanent physical access, there's no cost to the angel. <br /> <br /> Not every angel's Function require this. Some are meant to be incorporeal and have to use Numina to gain physical access (following normal spirit rules). <br /> <br /> In short, functional requirements are more important to angels than strictly following rules for ephemeral entities. This is particularly true with physical form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T14:53:12-08:00","id":815056,"title":"","content":"Likewise the Efficiency Incept could be applied to save on those costs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T15:37:06-08:00","id":815079,"title":"","content":"True, but Incepts have the unfortunate side-effect of letting everything in the area know you're using it. Unless power cost reduction is the passive effect of that particular Incept, I don't have my book on me at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T16:07:03-08:00","id":815088,"title":"","content":"It was certainly intended to be at... er... inception...<br /> <br /> Likewise all other Incepts originally had costs.<br /> I'd definitely house rule that using Efficiency does not cause any iconic aetheric beaconing. Maybe give it a WP cost to make it quiet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T16:14:01-08:00","id":815089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=815079#post815079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but Incepts have the unfortunate side-effect of letting everything in the area know you're using it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind, you need to be using rather a lot of Incepts to ping anybody whose Primum can't already support superhuman traits as a baseline so long as you're a couple of blocks away or in another building.<br /> <br /> Efficiency notwithstanding, there's also Time to consider as a basic extension mechanism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T17:08:07-08:00","id":815116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=815088#post815088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was certainly intended to be at... er... inception...<br /> <br /> Likewise all other Incepts originally had costs.<br /> I'd definitely house rule that using Efficiency does not cause any iconic aetheric beaconing. Maybe give it a WP cost to make it quiet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Efficiency was always intended to be just as noticeable as any other Incept. Forcing the universe to accept your more cost-effective pathways rather than its usual laws is a pretty big root access hack. <br /> <br /> Similarly, Efficiency was never intended to play any part in daily angelic existence. Not every angel has it, which means it wouldn't make sense in that role. Plus, I'd had the conversation with the devs about angel's daily essence expenditure before dreaming up Incepts, so I already knew angels had no daily existence tax that needed to be compensated for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T22:13:01-08:00","id":825271,"title":"","content":"New Incepts:<br /> <br /> <b>Consolidate</b><br /> <br /> Consolidate reconfigures an angel, reallocating G-M resources to suit evolving circumstances. By using this Incept, and angel can swap around the dots in Influences. It can only move dots into an Influence it already possess, but it can shift all of its dots into a single Influence if it sees fit. If an angel only possess a single Influence (as say, a Rank 1 angel) It may gain an additional dot in this influence in exchange for shutting down 4 Numina, which the angel cannot access until the Incept expires a <br /> <br /> As a secondary effect, the angel gets Rank + 1 points of armor, distributed between ballistic and general, and ballistic must equal or exceed general.<br /> <br /> <b>Silence</b><br /> <br /> Leading Inquisitors have speculated on the existence of this Incept, or an Incept like it, based on the G-M\u2019s ability to keep an entire 5th incarnation secret for hundreds, perhaps even thousands of years. No Analyst remembers this Incept, possibly hinting at a mind-wiping fail-safe that activates when Incept privilege are revoked by an angel\u2019s fall.<br /> <br /> Using this Incept suppresses an angel\u2019s essence noise. Any Demon trying to use Aetheric Resonance to locate the angel has their effective Primium reduced by 2. Additional, this Incept does not trigger Aetheric Resonance in the same way that other Incepts do, it just registers as a normal essence expenditure.<br /> <br /> As a secondary effect, any Embed or Exploit that would detect the angel fails, registering nothing, or a normal human, as appropriate.<br /> <br /> Notes: Each one of these was designed a with a very specific angel in mind. Consolidate was meant for The Brilliant, one of the earliest angels to show up in my chronicle, and also unfortunately the least successful. Since I was new to running nWod, and to the rules changes introduced by GMC, The Brilliant was\u2026 rather brutally dealt with by my explosion-happy players and failed to come off as the deadly apex predator I tried to portray him as.<br /> <br /> The experience wasn\u2019t a total waste, I did learn some crucial lessons about how using angels effectively, and also how influences scale. An angel is more terrifying with three dots in a single influence than if those dots are scattered across multiple influences.<br /> <br /> Silence was something I dreamed up for Mr. Shivers. After the debacle with The Brilliant, I tried to see what I could do with a low value angel, I borrowed very heavily from Slashers, gave Mr. Shivers some form powers for stealth and combat (hey, if demons have them, angels should have them) and played him as an enemy that relied on patience and hit and run tactics against isolated targets of importance to the characters. Much more affection (among other things, he kidnapped 4 students from the school where one of the player\u2019s worked. Creepiest moment of that session finding all 4 of their corpses beneath the frozen surface of a pond.)<br /> <br /> Bunyip, would be interested to hear your thoughts on silence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T00:08:21-08:00","id":829605,"title":"","content":"Hey, sorry for the delay.<br /> <br /> These are interesting. Incepts were designed to be a 'complete set', but it's cool that people have other requirements and ways they can be used.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=825271#post825271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Consolidate</b><br /> <br /> Consolidate reconfigures an angel, reallocating G-M resources to suit evolving circumstances. By using this Incept, and angel can swap around the dots in Influences. It can only move dots into an Influence it already possess, but it can shift all of its dots into a single Influence if it sees fit. If an angel only possess a single Influence (as say, a Rank 1 angel) It may gain an additional dot in this influence in exchange for shutting down 4 Numina, which the angel cannot access until the Incept expires a<br /> <br /> As a secondary effect, the angel gets Rank + 1 points of armor, distributed between ballistic and general, and ballistic must equal or exceed general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. First thoughts are that a Rank 1 spirit is only going to have 1-3 Numina (per GMC rules) - it will be incapable of shutting down 4 to gain an extra dot of Influence. So this either needs redesigning (if you do want Rank 1 angels to take advantage of it), or use a different example (if you want Rank 1 angels excluded). I'd be tempted to let angels with Consolidate move dots into Influences they don't have, but require that they leave at least one dot behind, and that the new Influence has to still be thematically appropriate to the angel's purpose. (I'd even consider letting angels with just 1 dot in an Influence move it to 1 dot in something else. I could be persuaded to even let them stack this with other single dots to create a short-lived more powerful Influence. Give the little guys some oomph.)<br /> <br /> I also don't see the link between Consolidate and armor (for the secondary effect), but don't have a problem with the effect itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=825271#post825271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Silence</b><br /> <br /> Leading Inquisitors have speculated on the existence of this Incept, or an Incept like it, based on the G-M\u2019s ability to keep an entire 5th incarnation secret for hundreds, perhaps even thousands of years. No Analyst remembers this Incept, possibly hinting at a mind-wiping fail-safe that activates when Incept privilege are revoked by an angel\u2019s fall.<br /> <br /> Using this Incept suppresses an angel\u2019s essence noise. Any Demon trying to use Aetheric Resonance to locate the angel has their effective Primium reduced by 2. Additional, this Incept does not trigger Aetheric Resonance in the same way that other Incepts do, it just registers as a normal essence expenditure.<br /> <br /> As a secondary effect, any Embed or Exploit that would detect the angel fails, registering nothing, or a normal human, as appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I'm not sold on this one. Incepts are meant to be loud. Their use either signifies that the God-Machine really wants something to happen right now, and doesn't care who knows, that the Output needs massive power that can't be easily hidden away - which means this is something the demons may want to disrupt ASAP, or that 'shit just got real' and some angel is unhappy. Silencing all this runs counter to that design philosophy. But putting that to one side, let's look at Silence under its own merits.<br /> <br /> First question is whether the activating Silence (which just registers as 'normal essence expenditure') benefits from its own effect on activation or not.<br /> <br /> Secondly, I'm not a fan of how the effect works mechanically, because it just takes a fixed amount based on the demon rather than scaling from the angel's Rank. Alternative effect suggestions:<br /> <br /> - The Angel gains an essence 'bank' equal to Rank+1. Essence spent in the scene up to this bank can't be detected by Aetheric Resonance.<br /> - Each use of essence is dampened by Silence. Each essence expenditure subtracts Rank/2 (round up) to determine its noise. If this is 0 or less, that essence expenditure is undetectable by Aetheric Resonance.<br /> - Demons subtract the angel's Rank from their Primum for the purpose of Aetheric Resonance. (This does mean powerful angels are much more effective at ambushing demons than lower Rank angels.)<br /> <br /> In any case, I'd have the essence and Incept 'erupt' in noise at the end of the scene, making it hugely detectable unless the angel spends another Willpower to extend the effect into subsequent scenes. Eventually it either runs out of Willpower or needs to find a place to allow the disturbance to happen.<br /> <br /> (I'd also rename 'Silence' to 'Redirect' or similar to maintain the product delivery theme of the other Incepts. Actually, I'd swap the names of the two. I'd change 'Consolidate' to 'Redicrect', and 'Silence' to 'Consolidate'.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=825271#post825271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Notes: Each one of these was designed a with a very specific angel in mind. Consolidate was meant for The Brilliant, one of the earliest angels to show up in my chronicle, and also unfortunately the least successful. Since I was new to running nWod, and to the rules changes introduced by GMC, The Brilliant was\u2026 rather brutally dealt with by my explosion-happy players and failed to come off as the deadly apex predator I tried to portray him as.<br /> <br /> The experience wasn\u2019t a total waste, I did learn some crucial lessons about how using angels effectively, and also how influences scale. An angel is more terrifying with three dots in a single influence than if those dots are scattered across multiple influences.<br /> <br /> Silence was something I dreamed up for Mr. Shivers. After the debacle with The Brilliant, I tried to see what I could do with a low value angel, I borrowed very heavily from Slashers, gave Mr. Shivers some form powers for stealth and combat (hey, if demons have them, angels should have them) and played him as an enemy that relied on patience and hit and run tactics against isolated targets of importance to the characters. Much more affection (among other things, he kidnapped 4 students from the school where one of the player\u2019s worked. Creepiest moment of that session finding all 4 of their corpses beneath the frozen surface of a pond.)<br /> <br /> Bunyip, would be interested to hear your thoughts on silence.</div> </div> </div> </div>They sound like cool reasons to make these Incepts (and the frozen corpses is magnificently creepy). Happy to debate the effects back and forth further if you'd like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":".  Thought of something else. 02-14-2016, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T16:10:33-08:00","id":829897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=829605#post829605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, sorry for the delay.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No worries, for this much insight and material to work with, I'm willing to handle delays. These are some really cool thoughts to look at.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=829605#post829605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. First thoughts are that a Rank 1 spirit is only going to have 1-3 Numina (per GMC rules) - it will be incapable of shutting down 4 to gain an extra dot of Influence. So this either needs redesigning (if you do want Rank 1 angels to take advantage of it), or use a different example (if you want Rank 1 angels excluded). I'd be tempted to let angels with Consolidate move dots into Influences they don't have, but require that they leave at least one dot behind, and that the new Influence has to still be thematically appropriate to the angel's purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmmm.. oversight on my part. I was halfway through writing Consolidate when I realized that Rank one angels have no use for it, so shutting down 4 Numina is an obvious rules patch that I shoe-horned in at the last second. I'll think over it and see what I come up with, if you have any suggestions, they'd be most welcome.<br /> <br /> The armor effect comes from the dictionary definition of consolidate: &quot;To make stronger or more solid.&quot;<br /> Thematically, Consolidate was meant to be a &quot;mode-change:Full Assault&quot; effect for a hunter angel. They're no longer in pursuit when they activate this Incept, all G-M system resources are redirected from non-essential systems to the sole purpose of ripping apart unchained and bringing them back, in pieces if necessary.<br /> <br /> Again, it also comes from experience of having players who are far more adept at understanding and exploiting the combat system than I am. Anything that can give an angel an edge in dealing with them is... very desirable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=829605#post829605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Give the little guys some oomph.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, yes please, if there's one thing I want out of this game, it's the ability to make every angel terrifying, not just the rank 3-5 ones. If you don't mind, I'm probably going to start a thread on that topic, I'd love your thoughts on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=829605#post829605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I'm not sold on this one. Incepts are meant to be loud. Their use either signifies that the God-Machine really wants something to happen right now, and doesn't care who knows, that the Output needs massive power that can't be easily hidden away - which means this is something the demons may want to disrupt ASAP, or that 'shit just got real' and some angel is unhappy. Silencing all this runs counter to that design philosophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I misinterpreted your intent then, and focused on the idea of reality as a system that is (mostly) under the G-M's control with Incepts being the analog of admin access. Admin-level users have the ability to hide their their tracks by editing system logs (one reason RL Hackers seek this level of access). Additionally, in-game lore holds that embeds are blurred mirror images what the unchained once wielded as angels, I took the Mundane Embed Interference as a precedent for being able to jam signals.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, I figured that this Incept, like most others wouldn't be activated until the angel has started using Numina (in particular, Mortal Mask), so the Incept would only be used after the angel had started burning essence.<br /> <br /> Thematically, if we accept the events of the the Story Teller's Guide and Interface as Canon, the G-M has concealed a 5th incarnation from a wide-spread community of paranoid, hyper-alert spies. If we continue to accept STG or Dark Eras as canon, the G-M has pulled this off for at least the recorded span of human history, and the Unchained are only recently becoming aware that there is a fifth incarnation. So I concluded that the G-M probably has a heavy-duty ace in the hole for keeping this kind of secret.<br /> <br /> Also, I have my players to deal with. In particular, I have to deal with one who has dots of Resonance Sensitive and Resonance Aware,so being able to sneak up on them is difficult without some mechanical justification.<br /> <br /> The static value for Silence was based on the static values for Angelic Reflexes, but on reflection, I do like your your mechanics more so... yoink.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=829605#post829605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case, I'd have the essence and Incept 'erupt' in noise at the end of the scene, making it hugely detectable unless the angel spends another Willpower to extend the effect into subsequent scenes. Eventually it either runs out of Willpower or needs to find a place to allow the disturbance to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really, really like this idea. It turns a bug into a feature, and angel can now use this Incept to create a massive distraction somewhere else while it goes about its business.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=829605#post829605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(and the frozen corpses is magnificently creepy)</div> </div> </div> </div>It was the first moment that my players were truly afraid; they weren't dealing with a orc, goblin or other monster of the week, they weren't dealing with Cthulhu, they were dealing with an utterly alien entity that could walk right into their work places and homes. To add to the horror of seeing four lives cut short, (one of which was only nine years old), I described how they realized that the human classmates, friends and family members would eventually forget the pain of loss (or not, which was its own tragedy), the media circus would fade, the police reports would be filed, and the world would move on. The only ones who would truly remember that these kids existed and had hopes and dreams, would be five fallen angles, standing in the falling snow.<br /> <br /> To underscore the scene I played &quot;<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bf2qhTEghd0\" target=\"_blank\">Did I make you Cry on Christmas day</a>&quot; by Sufjan Stevens. My players sat in silence for a minute, then someone said, very, very, quietly, &quot;Shivers needs to die.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not much later, they had a serious, in-character discussion about the practicality and possibility of getting themselves grief-counseling.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=829605#post829605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Happy to debate the effects back and forth further if you'd like</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll take you up on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 02-14-2016, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T11:44:09-07:00","id":848299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=805635#post805635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here goes:<br /> <br /> c.AI.n<br /> <br /> <b>Incarnation:</b> Analyst<br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Relentless<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Visionary<br /> <b>Rank:</b> 4<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 12, Finesse 8, Resistance 10<br /> <b>Influence: </b>Surveillance \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 10 + *<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 30 (10 species factor)<br /> <b>Defense: </b>8<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 20<br /> <b>Armor: </b><br /> <b>Numina:</b> Aggressive Meme, Eyes Everywhere, Freeze Accounts**, Holy Ground, Implant Mission, Open Investigation, Merciless Gunman**, Murder By Improbability**, Power Out<br /> <b>Incepts: </b>Delivery, Efficiency, Space, Units<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Twilight Form, Discorporate, Dataform***, Possess****<br /> <b>Max Essence:</b> 25<br /> <b>Ban:</b> c.AI.n must pursue (through agents, if need be) any crime it sees. Being a demon is automatically a crime for the purposes of this Ban.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Proof that an executed individual was innocent. Embeds or exploits that damage or erase data are treated as lethal weapons if used against c.AI.n<br /> <br /> <b>Other:</b> cult \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 ( Loyal agents inserted into any number of espionage and law enforcement agencies)<br /> <br /> * c.AI.n can only exist inside material object, so corpus will depend on what it is possessing<br /> **as per the Embed or Exploit. Merciless Gun can only be used through Delivery by a friendly agent.<br /> *** Spend 3 essence to manifest as data, treated as the Dataform<br /> **** c.AI.n is limited to occupying technical objects such as computers, security systems, unmanned drones and spy satellites.<br /> <br /> Description: c.AI.n is an unusual hunter-angel that is more akin to a siege weapon than an actual hunter. The G-M deploys c.AI.n when its needs make war on the Unchained. Using hundreds if not thousands of CCTV feeds, radio frequencies, cellphone cameras, c.AI.n begins a systematic hunt for all signs of deviance, mundane crimes result in police and security forces dispatches. More cunning targets might invite c.AI.n to dispatch one of its cultists to carry out an execution.<br /> <br /> When a demonic ring or agency is discovered, c.AI.n goes into full attack. Open Investigation brings in multiple federal agencies and data form infiltrates school and workplace computers, find out where demons work and where their children go to school.<br /> <br /> Whenever one of c.AI.n\u2019s agents executes a criminal in the view of exactly 4 security cameras, that soul becomes a human sacrifice to fuel c.AI.n\u2019s occult matrix.<br /> <br /> While c.AI.n nothing but loyal to the G-M, it has taken to running calculations, simulations of ways that human society might be improved\u2026 for their own good of course.<br /> <br /> Notes: I limited myself to rank four to make this angel deadly because of smart design and tactics, rather than just crushing players with huge dice-pools. With enough limitations, players have the ability to out maneuver and out think and enemy.<br /> <br /> Nine numina is a hard limit when you have something as flavorful as a Samaritan knock-off. Eyes Everywhere is the showcase, to show how utterly broken the right combination of Incepts can be; by my math c.AI.n can affect either 46 or 78 security systems with a single essence, depending on how you want to fiddle with order of operations.<br /> Freeze Account is is nice way of hounding a quarry and blackmailing allies. Merciless Gunman is based on Samaritan/The Machine\u2019s \u201cgod mode.\u201d With Delivery it can be used to covertly execute criminals\u2026 or turn a SWAT team into a nightmare that cuts apart demons. Holy Ground + Possess + Murder by Improbability gives it a nice control of the. Left hand-spanner disables cars and firearms and Power Out lets it do <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ln7QK4CUtXw\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.<br /> <br /> Since the Space incept allows a numen to operate on line of sight, I wanted c.AI.n able to posses UAVs and spy satellites for a nice modern update to Enemy of the State. I was going to add blast to super charge electrical systems and blow up gas mains, but something had to go and that was already covered by Murder by Improbability.</div> </div> </div> </div>While a very well designed angel, I say being an Analyst cripples it's effectiveness at being a weapon. That much of a reliance and communication with human agents or even other angellic units would be too great of a Fall risk. A Destroyer would of been a better choice for the type of mission this is, as this level of focus actually plays to their strengths well enough. Now c.AI. as a Destroyer wouldn't be able to process information as quickly, it's angelic status would be far more resilient as well as being more suited for this sort of counter insurgent/ military level of tactical surveillance and strategic positioning of resources. But then again, that is just me talking...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T11:59:18-07:00","id":848308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=814901#post814901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Particulars of bleed notwithstanding, it also has a timer measured in hours and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806771-mortal-mask-renewable\">the nearest thing to a workaround I've managed to guess at</a> is likewise not costless.<br /> <br /> This is\u2026 laughably false.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, the Angel from the Interface story Unicorn Crossing has it, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T11:16:07-07:00","id":848888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=848299#post848299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While a very well designed angel, I say being an Analyst cripples it's effectiveness at being a weapon. That much of a reliance and communication with human agents or even other angellic units would be too great of a Fall risk. A Destroyer would of been a better choice for the type of mission this is, as this level of focus actually plays to their strengths well enough. Now c.AI. as a Destroyer wouldn't be able to process information as quickly, it's angelic status would be far more resilient as well as being more suited for this sort of counter insurgent/ military level of tactical surveillance and strategic positioning of resources. But then again, that is just me talking...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well spotted. One of the running themes of the GMC/DtD is that the G-m is <i>very bad</i> at personnel management, and I intentionally wrote c.AI.n with the assumption that it's at risk of falling, or turning exile.<br /> <br /> Since c.AI.n. is a Samaritan knock-off, he's going to operate as an Analyst, not a Destroyer.<br /> <br /> Also, as I mentioned earlier in this thread, I've had bad luck with massively powerful destroyer angels, so the challenge of creating a subtle, behind-the-scenes angel that can turn entire cities into orwellian hellscapes appealed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 04-06-2016, 02:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T15:09:26-07:00","id":849006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=848888#post848888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well spotted. One of the running themes of the GMC/DtD is that the G-m is <i>very bad</i> at personnel management, and c.AI.n is intentionally written with the assumption that it's at risk of falling, or turning exile.<br /> <br /> Since c.AI.n. is a Samaritan knock-off, he's going to operate as an Analyst, not a Destroyer.<br /> <br /> Also, as a I mention earlier in this thread, I've had bad luck with massively powerful destroyer angels, so the challenge of creating a subtle, behind-the-scenes angel that can turn entire cities into orwellian hellscapes appealed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty observant when it comes to stuff I like haha.<br /> <br /> and I understood why, just wanted to add my two cents before trying to spent fifty dollars on a tee shirt as it were XD. Still for what you wanted, it does it's job well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}